# GET /catalog: every label, its URL, its sha256 and its abstract
route     GET /catalog
handler   catalog
memo      the contract of GET /catalog on tiesapi.com
input
  nothing
processing
  1 read the tie keywords: catalog/keywords.tsv
  2 read every named entry: catalog/entries/<name>, the operator's own words, byte-exact
  3 hash each entry's exact bytes; take its abstract: the title, and which of input, processing, output, graph it has
  4 list the objects by content address: catalog/objects/<64 hex>, when there are any
output
  200 {keywords, entries: [{entry, url, sha256, title, parts}], objects: [{id, url, title, parts}]}
  check: each sha256 equals the sha256 of GET /catalog/<entry> and of the file in git
graph
  the catalog in git (github.com/tiesapi/ties, catalog/entries/) is the public page content; drafts stay on the device
example
  GET /catalog
versions
